6. Full Cross-Subject Link Specification
6.1 Cross-Subject Link Schema
The cross-subject link schema defines the structure of a cross-subject link deposit.

It has the following fields:

link_id. A string. Required.

concept_name. A string. Required.

concept_description. A string. Required.

source_subject. A string. Required.

target_subject. A string. Required.

source_concept_name. A string. Required.

target_concept_name. A string. Required.

link_type. An enum. Required. The values are same_concept, analogous_concept, prerequisite, special_case, generalisation, other.

link_description. A string. Required.

link_direction. An enum. Required. The values are symmetric, source_to_target, target_to_source.

link_strength. An enum. Required. The values are strong, moderate, weak.

evidence. An array of evidence objects. Required.

age_range. An object. Optional. It contains min_age and max_age.

related_links. An array of link relations. Optional.

method_reference. A string. Optional.

learning_record_reference. A string. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each evidence object has:

evidence_id. A string.

source_reference. A string.

source_summary. A string.

evidence_type. An enum. The values are textbook, paper, lecture, curriculum, observation, other.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each link relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_link_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_concept, builds_on, related, alternative, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

