7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Cross-Subject Link
function createCrossSubjectLink(link, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the link against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the method reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the learning record reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. Generate a link ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 6. Insert the cross-subject link.

Step 7. Insert the evidence records and the link relations.

Step 8. Insert the method link and the learning link if present.

Step 9. Insert the provenance.

Step 10. Insert the moderation record.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the link_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Cross-Subject Link
function readCrossSubjectLink(linkId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the link. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the evidence, the link relations, the method link, the learning link, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Cross-Subject Link
function updateCrossSubjectLink(linkId, link, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing link. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new link.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the link_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Cross-Subject Link
function deleteCrossSubjectLink(linkId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing link. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the link_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Cross-Subject Links
function queryCrossSubjectLinks(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching links.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the links, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Cross-Subject Links
function aggregateCrossSubjectLinks(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching links.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the links and the count.

7.8 Export Cross-Subject Link
function exportCrossSubjectLink(linkId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each link, call createCrossSubjectLink.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching links.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per link. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Cross-Subject Link
function moderateCrossSubjectLink(linkId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing link. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the link_id and the status.

7.12 Cross-Subject Graph
function crossSubjectGraph(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all cross-subject links.

Step 3. Build the graph with concepts as nodes and links as edges, grouped by subject.

Step 4. Return the graph.

7.13 Subject Map
function subjectMap(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all cross-subject links.

Step 3. Build the map with subjects as regions and links as bridges.

Step 4. Return the map.

7.14 Concept Journey
function conceptJourney(conceptName, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all cross-subject links for the concept.

Step 3. Build the journey with the concept's appearance in each subject.

Step 4. Return the journey.

7.15 Link Strength View
function linkStrengthView(sourceSubject, targetSubject, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all cross-subject links between the two subjects.

